{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"A useful asymmetry emerged: when the top collector hooks a column beginning with its requested `8`, the adjacent `9` follows on retraction; when the left collector hooks a row beginning with the wrong `8`, the far `9` is left behind. I’m cross-checking the color/collector ownership rule on the opposite checker row and column before using it in a plan."}}
